:"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:24:53-07:00","id":1411666,"title":"","content":"And we funded project - in less than the hour! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What Streach Goals will Onyx Path bring to this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:25:53-07:00","id":1411667,"title":"","content":"The beginning paragraph about all Gods having once been mortals seems weird (hell, Sun Wukong is a stone monkey; he was never exactly human), and smells a bit like In Nomine's deliberate mess of a cosmology, but the rest is more than great enough to get the weird taste out.<br /> <br /> Good call on divine disabilities too (the text stops to point out how &quot;blindness that really doesn't affect the blind person&quot; isn't really blindness, and kind of insulting; it needs to an impediment <i>somehow, </i>otherwise it's not a disability).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:27:30-07:00","id":1411669,"title":"","content":"To be fair mortal doesn\u2019t necessarily mean human, it just means not a god, I assume","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:27:36-07:00","id":1411670,"title":"","content":"Wow. Not paying for shipping - it's almost the same price as the book! Guess I get PDF only, and hope I can find one at a store in future. Also hoping &quot;December 2022&quot; isn't the real shipping date...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:31:31-07:00","id":1411671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1411670#post1411670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Not paying for shipping - it's almost the same price as the book! Guess I get PDF only, and hope I can find one at a store in future. Also hoping &quot;December 2022&quot; isn't the real shipping date...</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't; OP deliberately overestimates how long things take to ship after the EX3 fiasco.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:36:16-07:00","id":1411675,"title":"","content":"It says ALMOST every god started as a mortal. It also has Fate doing a timey-wimey thing of having your new god having always been that god. It gets a bit brain-bendy for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:01:08-07:00","id":1411682,"title":"","content":"As noted on the Discord, there's something called a &quot;Cretin Bull.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm glad to see the Minotaur's embarrassing cousin get his time in the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:13:29-07:00","id":1411684,"title":"","content":"That's the name of one of the pledge tiers. It's the one which gets you a hardcover of each of the three books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T15:59:48-07:00","id":1411712,"title":"","content":"Damn they really knocked it out of the park with the preview, the disability section is particularly fantastic, it\u2019s just so good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T17:53:28-07:00","id":1411723,"title":"","content":"I also am curious if Demigod\u2019s gonna have the new Aggrevated tag that was shown off on the Discord server a long time ago","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:29:29-07:00","id":1411732,"title":"","content":"What's the new tag like? There is already an Aggravated tag in the Origin book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:36:26-07:00","id":1411733,"title":"","content":"One of the developers on the Scion discord said it was getting a revamp to make it more useful, specifically the revamped version deals damage that cannot be healed in any way in the middle of combat and ignores any armor that isn\u2019t logically resistant to the specific damage it deals, IE: Heaven\u2019s Fire would ignore any armor that isn\u2019t resistant to fire<br /> <br /> The specific text that was shared: Aggravated (2): This weapon deals grievous magical damage, such as a blade made of raw fire or lighting, or the revealed face of a God. Aggravated Injury Conditions may not be healed during a combat scene, whether by powers or spending Tension. If an antagonist has a regenerative effect, it cannot heal Aggravated damage. Armor does not apply against Aggravated damage unless it also has an appropriate Resistant Tag. This is meant expressly for magical and supernatural sources of injury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T23:48:45-07:00","id":1411748,"title":"","content":"In 12 hours we funded 200% of the campaign and got in to making <b>Demigod Companion</b>, with new powers, creatures and Guides for Pantheons! It looks GOOD as KS campaign of OPP, on my POV...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:18:01-07:00","id":1411775,"title":"","content":"Looking at the preview, it almost looks like you must assume some existing divinity\u2019s mantle to ascend. Am I reading that wrong ordid I miss something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:22:03-07:00","id":1411776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1411775#post1411775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the preview, it almost looks like you must assume some existing divinity\u2019s mantle to ascend. Am I reading that wrong ordid I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is how it seems to read to me too. That is disappointing if that is the case. My players will never go for assuming another identity of an already established god, they want to become their own gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:28:22-07:00","id":1411777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1411775#post1411775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the preview, it almost looks like you must assume some existing divinity\u2019s mantle to ascend. Am I reading that wrong ordid I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the intent. It's just that the process of adopting or taking the mantle of an existing God required more explanation, so it features more heavily in the text. If it's unclear (and you're not the first person to mention it), could you do me a favour and pop a comment into the feedback form to ask that becoming a separate God be emphasized more? It shouldn't take much rewriting to do, <br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> the guy who wrote the Apotheosis section","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:31:06-07:00","id":1411779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1411775#post1411775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the preview, it almost looks like you must assume some existing divinity\u2019s mantle to ascend. Am I reading that wrong ordid I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cA Demigod who wants to adopt the Mantle of an existing God is choosing a dangerous path to Apotheosis.\u201d<br /> <br /> so no, that is not the only path","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:32:46-07:00","id":1411780,"title":"","content":"It reads to me like that's just one of the ways. You can also build your own mantle based on your legend and deeds. However, they only really gave strong mechanics for when you're trying to steal a mantle from a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:36:35-07:00","id":1411798,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s probably because that\u2019s the one that requires the most mechanics, making your own Mantle is probably as easy as just going through an Apotheosis path like the one presented","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 09-04-2020, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:38:53-07:00","id":1411833,"title":"","content":"The segments going &quot;Follow this God's path&quot; I assume that you're trying to claim an existing Mantle. For forging your own, I think the intent is to focus on one's own Legend and forging it anew. But that could stand to be a bit clearer, yeah. If you see something you think could use clarification <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSev2R_ZUbt3ty5TIniJI61YboDEgwzaeNmUwQVev3j6qhAxXw/viewform\" target=\"_blank\">mention it here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-04-2020, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T21:28:05-07:00","id":1412000,"title":"","content":"I think I am most interested in the new pantheons, particularly the Mesopotamian gods. Ishtar I am looking at you. I am curious how they discuss their various mantles and associations with cities in some cases. Though the first chapter is the chapter I didn't know I wanted. The path to ascension was never really talked about in the 1st edition so this is good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T21:43:07-07:00","id":1412002,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m more curious about the Apu and Tengri personally for the pantheons, also curious about the new Birthrights like the Sancta","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T23:51:02-07:00","id":1412012,"title":"","content":"I want to see that Anunna and the Atua, personally. I have a potential Scion of Ishtar I'd like to stat up.<br /> <br /> I've seen a comment from someone familiar with Ishtar say something like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good news [about being a Scion of Ishtar]! She wants nothing more than for you to go out and do what you think is best. But she also would want you to keep out of HER way </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T01:02:06-07:00","id":1412021,"title":"","content":"As agnostic with slight Slavic neopagan bent, I'm curious over Bogovi, of course. But as Bogovi sounds almost like general Polish word for gods - 'Bogowie' - I will most surely use old Slavic name for those beings as Pantheon - Bogi.<br /> <br /> You know, to not have this word nightmare on sessions: 'I przybyli Bogovi i inni Bogowie.' \ud83d\ude14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T01:34:35-07:00","id":1412024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412021#post1412021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As agnostic with slight Slavic neopagan bent, I'm curious over Bogovi, of course. But as Bogovi sounds almost like general Polish word for gods - 'Bogowie' - I will most surely use old Slavic name for those beings as Pantheon - Bogi.<br /> <br /> You know, to not have this word nightmare on sessions: 'I przybyli Bogovi i inni Bogowie.' \ud83d\ude14</div> </div> </div> </div>Bogovi is actually the older form, from Old Church Slavonic. It later shifted to the simpler form &quot;Bogi&quot; in several Slavic languages, e.g. Russian. So for an attempt to reconstruct a pre-Christian Slavic Pantheon, Bogovi might in fact be more fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:56:41-07:00","id":1412054,"title":"","content":"All the names of the pantheons means basically gods in their mother languages, at least it\u2019s what I understand from what I know, Theoi, Kami, Orisha, Aesir, etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, Kami and Orisha are a bit more \u201copen ended\u201d as they represent spirits in general, with some more complex versions of the name meaning Great Spirits, the ones that we see in the books. But it\u2019s related to the definition of god...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-05-2020, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T05:25:24-07:00","id":1412058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412054#post1412054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the names of the pantheons means basically gods in their mother languages, at least it\u2019s what I understand from what I know, Theoi, Kami, Orisha, Aesir, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, you are right - but modern languages do not interlope the same like Bogovi and 'Bogowie' in Polish. ( Which is spelled 'Bogovi-E' in English spelling. ) I do not suspect that modern Greeks are talking about One God as Theo, on day to day basis, for example. So they not invoking 'One God and Olumpian Gods' as 'Theos and Theoi Olympion', on day-to-day basis. ( But I'm not modern Greek speaker, so what should I know... )<br /> <br /> Also, Aesir are <i>one family</i> of Norse Gods - other are Vanir, for example. And you have Jotuun as Giants. It makes desctinction much profound in day to day language on game sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2020, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:03:00-07:00","id":1412072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412058#post1412058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally, you are right - but modern languages do not interlope the same like Bogovi and 'Bogowie' in Polish. ( Which is spelled 'Bogovi-E' in English spelling. ) I do not suspect that modern Greeks are talking about One God as Theo, on day to day basis, for example. So they not invoking 'One God and Olumpian Gods' as 'Theos and Theoi Olympion', on day-to-day basis. ( But I'm not modern Greek speaker, so what should I know... )<br /> <br /> Also, Aesir are <i>one family</i> of Norse Gods - other are Vanir, for example. And you have Jotuun as Giants. It makes desctinction much profound in day to day language on game sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>God (as in the Christian God) in modern Greek is <i>Theos</i>, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T10:24:38-07:00","id":1412110,"title":"","content":"I really like the Annunua snippets in the new update, the writing\u2019s so good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T10:26:47-07:00","id":1412112,"title":"","content":"I think the Me might be one of my favorite pantheon Relic ideas, so cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:13:05-07:00","id":1412131,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned from time to time that I have a concept for a Scion of Ishtar. Having read Ishtar's write-up, I'm more convinced that the biggest problem they would have towards getting along would be that Ishtar and Aaliyah (my character concept) are, in some ways, far too similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:15:44-07:00","id":1412132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412110#post1412110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the Annunua snippets in the new update, the writing\u2019s so good</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like it, too. But I hope they reprint the Tyrant Calling in Demigod or else one is forced to buy Titanomachy, which is not of the three Core ones, to use Ereshkigal to the fullest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:35:29-07:00","id":1412137,"title":"","content":"Read Anunna preview - they all seem very much on 'love' ( all of them are Lovers, beside Marduk), but Enki sets new low with impregnating his wife, daughter and granddaughter - and then impregnating himself. Interesting way to create new gods dynasty, I must admit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2020, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:36:16-07:00","id":1412138,"title":"","content":"P. S. I love trans woman support in Ishtar write-up! \u2764\ufe0f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:36:29-07:00","id":1412139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackLotos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412132#post1412132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like it, too. But I hope they reprint the Tyrant Calling in Demigod or else one is forced to buy Titanomachy, which is not of the three Core ones, to use Ereshkigal to the fullest.</div> </div> </div> </div>eh, it\u2019s easy enough to replace with Leader if you don\u2019t have it, rather than using word count on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:38:12-07:00","id":1412140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412137#post1412137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read Annanua preview - they all seem very much on 'love' ( all of them are Lovers, beside Marduk), but Enki sets new low with impregnating his wife, daughter and granddaughter - and then impregnating himself. Interesting way to create new gods dynasty, I must admit...</div> </div> </div> </div>This one thanks the Gender Fluid idea to another level! But they are not alone, Loki having mothered some of his kids is an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:48:53-07:00","id":1412142,"title":"","content":"Enki's ability to impregnate himself isn't genderfluidity - he's very firmly male, all the time, no matter what. That was rather the problem he had when he impregnated himself, actually.<br /> <br /> (Ishtar/Inanna is closer to genderfluidity, though she weighs heavily female regardless of presentation. Gender as it relates to the Ishtar cult is complex but the modern world would absolutely see some of her priestesses as trans women, so I felt it was important to write that support into her.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:55:38-07:00","id":1412145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412139#post1412139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> eh, it\u2019s easy enough to replace with Leader if you don\u2019t have it, rather than using word count on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the book should spell that out or else some people could be very confused about the Calling they might have never seen before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:15:28-07:00","id":1412150,"title":"","content":"So that Anunna update is interesting. I would not have pegged Ishtar for having Epic Strength or Epic Dexterity, but rather Sky and Stars instead. Mesopotamian myth is complex though because of how old it is. I admit I am not a scholar and may not know the full stories of her existence. I also would have pegged her for a Liminal calling instead of a Trickster, but the line can be fine for that and I can see both sides of the coin. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:17:11-07:00","id":1412151,"title":"","content":"I remember hearing that the Titan Callings will have their description reprinted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:25:30-07:00","id":1412154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412150#post1412150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that Anunna update is interesting. I would not have pegged Ishtar for having Epic Strength or Epic Dexterity, but rather Sky and Stars instead. Mesopotamian myth is complex though because of how old it is. I admit I am not a scholar and may not know the full stories of her existence. I also would have pegged her for a Liminal calling instead of a Trickster, but the line can be fine for that and I can see both sides of the coin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason Ishtar does not have Stars is that, essentially, we had to decide if we wanted to give everyone Stars. Almost all of the Anunna have a star or planet associated with them! Ultimately, we settled on that being left to the three elder gods over the rest. Ishtar's a war goddess and a warrior herself, with exceptional strength and speed demonstrated in some of her stories, and she doesn't really have a ton of weather associations...but overall, the Anunna were hard to narrow down Purviews for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:43:20-07:00","id":1412157,"title":"","content":"What stories are those? I love reading about those ancient myths. Is there a recommended source for them? Thanks for the insight. I suspected it might be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:48:12-07:00","id":1412158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412157#post1412157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What stories are those? I love reading about those ancient myths. Is there a recommended source for them? Thanks for the insight. I suspected it might be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Sumerian texts can be found here: <a href=\"http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/\" target=\"_blank\">http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:55:41-07:00","id":1412160,"title":"","content":"The specific story I'm thinking of is Inana and Ebih, where Ishtar/Inana gets very angry at a mountain and kills it with a mix of her terrifying archery (which also involves a lot of stone hail and silt flood, but I take that in this case to be metaphor or special effects for her power rather than something that'd require Sky or Water) and knife fighting.<br /> <br /> Mountains have necks, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T14:21:25-07:00","id":1412164,"title":"","content":"Classic Inanna. She is one angry lady.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T14:47:30-07:00","id":1412167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412164#post1412164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Classic Inanna. She is one angry lady.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inanna wouldn't get angry if there weren't so many people PISSING HER OFF! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T16:36:25-07:00","id":1412184,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading the Annuna snippet. Love it! Glad to see my boys are being well-represented. <br /> <br /> I would argue that, if a Goddess has a well-known title like &quot;Queen of Heaven,&quot; she probably qualifies for the Stars Purview, and I've always heard of her being described as a Sky Goddess as well. But, who cares? If I think she should have those, I can give her two more Purviews all by myself.<br /> <br /> I'm a big boy, now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T22:21:36-07:00","id":1412220,"title":"","content":"As to 'Titans uncertainty', there is direct pointing in Demigod Preview 1 about Demigods taking Titan Callings - <br /> 'Titans on the Threshold<br /> While completing the Threshold Deed, a Demigod can choose to take on any of the Titanic Callings from Titanomachy as part of his progress. If he still has any of those Callings when he completes the Milestone, however, it becomes a fixed part of his character and will cause other legendary beings to treat him accordingly.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T23:09:51-07:00","id":1412224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412220#post1412220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to 'Titans uncertainty', there is direct pointing in Demigod Preview 1 about Demigods taking Titan Callings -<br /> 'Titans on the Threshold<br /> While completing the Threshold Deed, a Demigod can choose to take on any of the Titanic Callings from Titanomachy as part of his progress. If he still has any of those Callings when he completes the Milestone, however, it becomes a fixed part of his character and will cause other legendary beings to treat him accordingly.'</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You have a Titanic Calling.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah so do half the Anunna and most of the Atua. Shiva and Kali are Destroyers. The fuck's your point?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Disclaimer: Yes I realize that neither Shiva nor Kali in the corebook have the Destroyer Calling, but that is very likely due to &quot;Destroyer didn't exist when they were being written&quot; and I'll personally be treating Shiva as having Destroyer from here on out because <i>d'uh</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T04:22:50-07:00","id":1412254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412224#post1412224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;You have a Titanic Calling.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah so do half the Anunna and most of the Atua. Shiva and Kali are Destroyers. The fuck's your point?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth it just to watch the kid with the Destroyer calling sitting in a tree, picking his teeth with the tip of his knife, watching his detractor getting pasted by some big, scaly horror and just calling down.<br /> <br /> &quot;You doing OK down there, cupcake?&quot;<br /> <br /> And pointedly not representing. Not until they ask. Really, really nicely.<br /> <br /> How else is a guy gonna get respect for doing what nobody else wants to do? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T05:09:42-07:00","id":1412261,"title":"","content":"I'm deeply confused about The Descent. We're supposed to resolve a strength 5 fatebinding in such a way that takes the mortal out of play - despite the fact that strength 5 fatebindings explicitly can't be resolved in that way: they're supposed to endure beyond death after all. Is there some kind of exception to the rule callout I'm missing here? It feels like the intent is that the new SGC is supposed to be truly gone, not 'just' lingering as a ghost but there's nothing in the text to make it clear how this is supposed to go, that could just be my read..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T06:47:40-07:00","id":1412271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412261#post1412261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm deeply confused about The Descent. We're supposed to resolve a strength 5 fatebinding in such a way that takes the mortal out of play - despite the fact that strength 5 fatebindings explicitly can't be resolved in that way: they're supposed to endure beyond death after all. Is there some kind of exception to the rule callout I'm missing here? It feels like the intent is that the new SGC is supposed to be truly gone, not 'just' lingering as a ghost but there's nothing in the text to make it clear how this is supposed to go, that could just be my read..</div> </div> </div> </div>When a Fatebinding is Resolved, it's Resolved. The Fatebinding Duration represents how long it will last before fading on its own. Resolving it supercedes that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:05:02-07:00","id":1412273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412271#post1412271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a Fatebinding is Resolved, it's Resolved. The Fatebinding Duration represents how long it will last before fading on its own. Resolving it supercedes that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, firstly apologies for getting the term wrong. This is the Parting, not the Descent. That said, Strength 5 Fatebindings have an exemption to the resolution thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion Hero p197</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Strength 5 Fatebindings last even beyond the death or apotheosis of either party; if the Scion\u2019s player creates a new character who is the reincarnation of her previous character, the Fatebinding transfers over. Likewise, if the Fatebound mortal dies, his ghost wakes in the Underworld of the Scion\u2019s pantheon and remains Fatebound \u2014 though at the Storyguide\u2019s discretion, the SGC\u2019s role might change (usually, though not always, to Jinx, Nemesis, or Rival). <b>The Fatebound character may never be removed from play by the resolution of a role Condition</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering if Demigod has a specific exemption to that, or if I'm misunderstanding something. But AFAICT it's just a contradiction as presented. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Preview p19</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Milestone for the Parting stage requires a character to build up a new Fatebinding to Strength 5, then Resolve it. It has to be a new Fatebinding (with a role chosen from one of the Scion\u2019s Callings), but it can either be with an established SGC or with a new one introduced for the purpose. This bond doesn\u2019t count against the maximum number of Fatebindings a character can have. Each time it is Invoked, the Strength increases by 1 automatically at the beginning of the next session. <b>The Resolution must take a form that removes the SGC from play permanently</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:08:32-07:00","id":1412275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412273#post1412273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if Demigod has a specific exemption to that, or if I'm misunderstanding something. But AFAICT it's just a contradiction as presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be inclined to treat it as an exception to the general rule. It adds more dramatic weight if the person who you thought was <i>always</i> going to be there, even beyond death, is now gone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:37:38-07:00","id":1412278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412275#post1412275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be inclined to treat it as an exception to the general rule. It adds more dramatic weight if the person who you thought was <i>always</i> going to be there, even beyond death, is now gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm. I'm unsure - you're right of course, but that runs the risk of that person and their interractions having less weight. Like, maybe keep the bond on the sheet but move the character out of play, so it's some kind of Banquo's Ghost effect, where they're not full on there but are a part of the story that sticks with you....<br /> <br /> *shrugs* I guess I'd case by case it, personally. I'm just curious of the intent, and of any other ways to handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:43:05-07:00","id":1412280,"title":"","content":"Huh, I'd forgotten the whole &quot;Cannot be resolved at Strength 5&quot; and I'll probably go back to forgetting it because it doesn't make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> And yeah, in this case I'd say that the rules for the Parting supercede the rules of Fatebinding Endurance, as one of the more general rules is &quot;Specific Trumps General&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:51:29-07:00","id":1412281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412280#post1412280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I'd forgotten the whole &quot;Cannot be resolved at Strength 5&quot; and I'll probably go back to forgetting it because it doesn't make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> And yeah, in this case I'd say that the rules for the Parting supercede the rules of Fatebinding Endurance, as one of the more general rules is &quot;Specific Trumps General&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea behind it is that you and that person will always be tied somehow. You can shift the nature of that relationship through resolving the bond, but this is a person who will always be with you in some form. It's the 'across incarnations love story' option, or the Solar/Lunar bond linked to souls rather than Exaltations if you prefer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T08:13:02-07:00","id":1412289,"title":"","content":"But yeah, for the purposes of the Parting, I'd say the &quot;Remove the character from play for this step&quot; supersedes the &quot;Strength 5 Fatebindings cannot be removed from play&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T08:22:06-07:00","id":1412290,"title":"","content":"I think the Parting is the one exception in the future god life, when you can actually break this rule permanently.<br /> <br /> I would say more, to the character perspective, that one ghost of their love/family/what ever that keep they comfortable for knowing they would be there for ever suddenly be removed from the story for good is the real meaning of parting.<br /> <br /> Losing that one admirer or that one unlucky guy that is always getting himself in trouble around them is almost a relief...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T07:44:30-07:00","id":1412436,"title":"","content":"The Apu look great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T12:18:26-07:00","id":1412460,"title":"","content":"I know basically nothing about the Inca nor their mythology but the Apu preview looks really great, yeah! Definitely loved the origin of everything blurb at the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T19:17:47-07:00","id":1412514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412460#post1412460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know basically nothing about the Inca nor their mythology but the Apu preview looks really great, yeah! Definitely loved the origin of everything blurb at the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only know small snippets picked up over the years, but yes, they look really cool. <br /> <br /> Also got to read the Mesopotamian preview, which also looked pretty fun. Very much looking forward to this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T03:48:14-07:00","id":1412561,"title":"","content":"Waiting for new Pantheons manuscript preview - *Refresh. Refresh. Refresh. Refresh. Refresh. Refresh...*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T05:24:32-07:00","id":1412572,"title":"","content":"New Pantheons are up!<br /> <br /> And yeah, the Titanic Callings are now explictly had by several members in most of the pantheons. Hell, they even went back and said &quot;okay, here are some Gods from Hero who should have Titanic Callings, but they weren't made yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, they explicitly note that the Titanic Callings are ultimately that because they support a God's Purviews rather than the other way around; Agni is a Primeval because his job has to do with Fire itself, not because he's necessarily a misanthrope, Ereshkigal is a Tyrant because she cares not for the dead themselves, only the cycle of life, but within that she is honest and dedicated to her duty. However, because a Titanic Calling is focused on the Purview, it <i>can </i>lead to an inhuman perspective, because by definition, it forgets humans much of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T09:17:23-07:00","id":1412607,"title":"","content":"One problem: The Atua lack example Birthrights.<br /> <br /> Which is a shame, because everything else about them rules, from their environmental focus to them legendarily not getting what the big difference between Gods and Titans are (and later becoming sure they were right the first time), to Tangaroa's &quot;wait, my kids are sentient?&quot; approach to parenting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T09:20:16-07:00","id":1412608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412607#post1412607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem: The Atua lack example Birthrights.<br /> <br /> Which is a shame, because everything else about them rules, from their environmental focus to them legendarily not getting what the big difference between Gods and Titans are (and later becoming sure they were right the first time), to Tangaroa's &quot;wait, my kids are sentient?&quot; approach to parenting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am positive we will see a Relic stretchgoal for the Companion, so hopefully some Atua stuff can go there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T09:36:15-07:00","id":1412610,"title":"","content":"It is weird the Atua don\u2019t have any sample Birthrights, when the other two pantheons in the preview do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T09:39:09-07:00","id":1412611,"title":"","content":"The Count of Words is a harsh taskmaster, and it's possible that there was a section but it had to get cut to make room for the four Sisters of Mauna Kea or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T09:52:22-07:00","id":1412613,"title":"","content":"And hopefully that is something they can use the Companion stretchgoal Brithrights to make up for. I'm sure we'll see a Relics expansion as we've gotten the other core ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T00:21:26-07:00","id":1412809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412024#post1412024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bogovi is actually the older form, from Old Church Slavonic. It later shifted to the simpler form &quot;Bogi&quot; in several Slavic languages, e.g. Russian. So for an attempt to reconstruct a pre-Christian Slavic Pantheon, Bogovi might in fact be more fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick - Old Chruch Slavonic is still younger than <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Slavic\" target=\"_blank\">Proto-Slavic</a> - like at least 5 centuries younger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bogovi preview points that each God in Pantheon is called Bog ( that is Proto- and Modern Slavic ), but in Polish, it can be simpler Bogi as plural. However, I'm glad that the Pantheon preview just came out and I'm delving into it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T00:33:13-07:00","id":1412813,"title":"","content":"Little errata for the Bogovi write-up, on Underworld: <i><b>Peklo \u2013 The Underworld</b><br /> When one mentions the Underworld, they usually think of two separate and diametrically opposed places: heaven or hell. Peklo, however, is both. How it appears to any singular spirit depends on how they carried out their lives. Those who lived in accordance to their nature and upheld their honor and duty find themselves in Raj \u2013 a warm and lush, heavenly paradise where they want for nothing. Those who failed to uphold their honor and duty, however, experience not fire and brimstone as one would equate a hellish landscape; <b>Nav</b> is a dreary, frozen wasteland which falls under Veles\u2019 personal dominion</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>.</i><br /> <br /> In text about Peklo ( <i>Piek\u0142o</i>, in Polish, I assume ), it mention <i>Nav</i>, realm of spirit, as description of Peklo itself. So Nav should be changed for Peklo here.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-10-2020, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T00:38:00-07:00","id":1412815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412813#post1412813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little errata for the Bogovi write-up, on Underworld: <i><b>Peklo \u2013 The Underworld</b><br /> When one mentions the Underworld, they usually think of two separate and diametrically opposed places: heaven or hell. Peklo, however, is both. How it appears to any singular spirit depends on how they carried out their lives. Those who lived in accordance to their nature and upheld their honor and duty find themselves in Raj \u2013 a warm and lush, heavenly paradise where they want for nothing. Those who failed to uphold their honor and duty, however, experience not fire and brimstone as one would equate a hellish landscape; <b>Nav</b> is a dreary, frozen wasteland which falls under Veles\u2019 personal dominion</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>.</i><br /> <br /> In text about Peklo ( <i>Piek\u0142o</i>, in Polish, I assume ), it mention <i>Nav</i>, realm of spirit, as description of Peklo itself. So Nav should be changed for Peklo here.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the Feedback Form is for: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSev2R_ZUbt3ty5TIniJI61YboDEgwzaeNmUwQVev3j6qhAxXw/viewform\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1F...hAxXw/viewform</a><br /> <br /> But good find. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T00:45:32-07:00","id":1412816,"title":"","content":"I get it right that Thrice-Tenth Kingdom is Terra Incognita in terms of <b>Scion</b> cosmology categorization? I.E. 'Secret' realm inside Material Plane of the World?<br /> <br /> <i><b>The Thrice-Tenth Kingdom</b><br /> Existing as both its own realm but outside of the world tree proper, the Thrice-Tenth Kingdom is a heroic plane where fairytales transpire, heroes make their mark, and gods walk elbow to elbow with mortals. Nothing is too out of the ordinary in this place, and one can easily cross over into it unwittingly and find themselves in part of a story they heard in their childhood. Deep in the forests of the Thrice-Tenth Kingdom, however, is where Baba Yaga makes her home and rules over it from her chicken-legged hut.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T04:43:50-07:00","id":1412831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412816#post1412816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get it right that Thrice-Tenth Kingdom is Terra Incognita in terms of <b>Scion</b> cosmology categorization? I.E. 'Secret' realm inside Material Plane of the World?</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand it\u2019s another reality, or at least another world, much like the 9 worlds of Yggdrasil are not in Earth. The 3x10th kindom is an separated world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T07:58:12-07:00","id":1412849,"title":"","content":"I use Terra Incognita as a catch-all term for &quot;Weird Place&quot;, to be honest. Like I ignore a lot of the classification of Axis Mundi and Touchstone for the most part because a lot of attempts at classification run headlong into examples that break the classifications because turns out a lot of human cultures didn't meet up in order to come up with a unified cosmology.<br /> <br /> The Thrice-Tenth Kingdom could be a place that you can get to by walking into a spooky forest that isn't on any map, it could be a separate place, it COULD be a separate realm that tenuously links to the mundane World. Does it really matter <i>exactly</i> if it's a separate dimension or if it happens to be an odd place in the World that you can't see unless you're inside it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T14:01:50-07:00","id":1412898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412849#post1412849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thrice-Tenth Kingdom could be a place that you can get to by walking into a spooky forest that isn't on any map, it could be a separate place, it COULD be a separate realm that tenuously links to the mundane World. Does it really matter <i>exactly</i> if it's a separate dimension or if it happens to be an odd place in the World that you can't see unless you're inside it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself wanting to put Castle Dracula in 3x10. And then have the PCs stop by while he is hosting Baba Yaga for afternoon tea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T21:45:15-07:00","id":1412961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1412898#post1412898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find myself wanting to put Castle Dracula in 3x10. And then have the PCs stop by while he is hosting Baba Yaga for afternoon tea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would give a lot to be in that scene. If you ever do it pleasepleaseplease post the outcome here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T04:30:36-07:00","id":1412984,"title":"","content":"The Thrice Tenth Kingdom also has the Firebird. Weren't its feathers healing charms? As with &quot;The Forest Called Dark Night of the Soul&quot; and all those Celtic forests you entered while chasing a white deer across a stream, there are treasures hidden along with the wonders and traps. <br /> <br /> Don't forget to set up tasty lures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-12-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T06:12:26-07:00","id":1412998,"title":"","content":"The Tengri in the new preview are super good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T06:38:03-07:00","id":1413002,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile for the Bogovi I\u2019m still unsure of but I do know I hate Veles, that line about stealing Scions\u2019 smartphones to teach them the world around them is more important is just peak boomer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T10:08:15-07:00","id":1413053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413002#post1413002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile for the Bogovi I\u2019m still unsure of but I do know I hate Veles, that line about stealing Scions\u2019 smartphones to teach them the world around them is more important is just peak boomer</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Good. Good. All according to plan.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.erykahfassett.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, serif\"><b>Erykah Fassett</b></span></a><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The closer you get to the light, the greater your shadow becomes.&quot;</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms","name":"ShadowBlossoms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24398_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T13:38:06-07:00","id":1413090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413002#post1413002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile for the Bogovi I\u2019m still unsure of but I do know I hate Veles, that line about stealing Scions\u2019 smartphones to teach them the world around them is more important is just peak boomer</div> </div> </div> </div>I only know Veles from some folk stories and previous Polish Slavic RPG - but Veles seem to be much more this 'serious, Underworld ( and cattle) guy', like Hades for Greeks - than this 'weird Trickster guy' from Scion. On the other hand, Veles IS often equated with Dragon, so some Trickery - or being Scion Dragon - may works from my oral sources... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T15:40:33-07:00","id":1413119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413090#post1413090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I only know Veles from some folk stories and previous Polish Slavic RPG - but Veles seem to be much more this 'serious, Underworld ( and cattle) guy', like Hades for Greeks - than this 'weird Trickster guy' from Scion. On the other hand, Veles IS often equated with Dragon, so some Trickery - or being Scion Dragon - may works from my oral sources... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can take him as trickster up with Vyacheslav Ivanov and Vladimir Toporov as those appear to be the main Bogovi sources being leaned on here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T16:51:09-07:00","id":1413128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413002#post1413002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile for the Bogovi I\u2019m still unsure of but I do know I hate Veles, that line about stealing Scions\u2019 smartphones to teach them the world around them is more important is just peak boomer</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't some gods be peak Boomer (speaking as a Boomer born in 1960)? Gods can be timeless or deeply concerned to a given time. Some gods would be eternally of your grandparents generation, no matter when that was. Also, if a deity's trickster form is about forcing you to go beyond your subconscious limits, wouldn't they act like those you see as the enemy? <br /> <br /> Some Scions who pride themselves on being (place in fashion term for aware of zeitgeist of the moment) would have to face seriously unwoke adversaries. As a child of the 1960s and 70s, if I met the same kind of being, they would probably appear to me as a deeply racist misogynist. Because of how important the issues of race and sex were in those decades. This even though most of the people on these boards tend to lable me a racist misogynist.<br /> <br /> Note: I have been against both racism and misogyny since my childhood experiences with people (including close friends and family members) being grossly victimized by racists and misogynists. I just see about 90% of being &quot;Woke&quot; as counterproductive and deeply destructive to any progressive movement in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-11-2020, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T17:58:36-07:00","id":1413139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413002#post1413002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile for the Bogovi I\u2019m still unsure of but I do know I hate Veles, that line about stealing Scions\u2019 smartphones to teach them the world around them is more important is just peak boomer</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I've always pictured some of the older Slavic gods like Veles or Stribog as very much in the &quot;grumpy old grampa&quot; archetype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T18:09:19-07:00","id":1413140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413119#post1413119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can take him as trickster up with Vyacheslav Ivanov and Vladimir Toporov as those appear to be the main Bogovi sources being leaned on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods associated with magicians and sorcerers (Hermes, Odin, Veles) seem to have a trend for also being considered tricksters. Sort of the same way thunder gods (Zeus, Thor, Indra) tend to be very macho and like to swing their ... thunderbolts around a lot. I'm sure there's probably an anthropology paper or three on the subject out there somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T09:03:24-07:00","id":1413242,"title":"","content":"The new Stretch Goals look real neat, I\u2019m especially looking forward to the new Cult one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T02:43:13-07:00","id":1413741,"title":"","content":"We have new <b>Demigod</b> public preview on Legend trait - and it shows more canonical information on Scions status in the World - <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/scion-demigod-book-3-for-the-scion-second-edition-rpg/posts/2953433\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2953433</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T06:02:14-07:00","id":1413760,"title":"","content":"The new preview\u2019s our and I love how buffed up all the base Birthrights, and I love the new Realm Birthright","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T06:53:42-07:00","id":1413763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413760#post1413760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new preview\u2019s our and I love how buffed up all the base Birthrights, and I love the new Realm Birthright</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah the Realm Birthright is a surprise! I knew Sanctum was going to be a thing, but not Realm and Realm Knacks.<br /> <br /> Now we know what Hades' done with those barely fitting Calling dots - he's stacked them with Hades-Realm Knacks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-19-2020, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T13:27:47-07:00","id":1413828,"title":"","content":"Really need to get a &quot;how to create a balanced knack&quot; section in one of these books. It'd be all guidelines, but still, it would make my anxiety shut up whenever I try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T16:01:01-07:00","id":1413862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413828#post1413828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really need to get a &quot;how to create a balanced knack&quot; section in one of these books. It'd be all guidelines, but still, it would make my anxiety shut up whenever I try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, some advice I learned from my homebrewing.<ul><li>If it feels too weak to be a Boon, but definitely too powerful to be a basic thing you can get from a set of tools or something, it's probably a Knack.</li> <li>Don't be afraid to make Knacks situational.</li> <li>Remember, for utility: The iGjallar's ability to get a signal anywhere and never run out of batteries</li> <li>This one is for Homebrewing in general: Sometimes you may make something far stronger than you intended. If this happens, that's okay, that's what testing is for. <i>You can adjust it</i> after the fact. If your Knack accidentally shatters combat balance, you can reduce its power<ul><li>To play off this: You're not designing Knacks for sale, generally. Consider its use at your table to be the playtesting phase.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Basically... Sometimes Knack Balance is something you pick up. And it's okay to make mistakes at your table when homebrewing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-16-2020, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T19:10:01-07:00","id":1414121,"title":"","content":"I am not entirely sure how I feel about several of the Relics in the previews just giving you extra Boons, on the one hand it\u2019s not like you have a ton of Legend even at Legend 8, but on the other hand it does make the benefits of Specialized Purviews in Companion far weaker, and cheapens the whole concept of Boon slots in the first place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T05:26:41-07:00","id":1414182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414121#post1414121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not entirely sure how I feel about several of the Relics in the previews just giving you extra Boons, on the one hand it\u2019s not like you have a ton of Legend even at Legend 8, but on the other hand it does make the benefits of Specialized Purviews in Companion far weaker, and cheapens the whole concept of Boon slots in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there was much talk about Relics that offered Boons when Mysteries of the World (Hero Companion) was dropped. While i don't remember a compromise anyone agreed too, I think that one of the better regarded ones was that Relic Boons 'occupied' a Boon slot. I disagreed then, (and to be honest, with you) saying that it is hardly a major issue and having the Relic 'eat' a Boon slot cheapens boons.<br /> On specialized Purviews, i would like to note that while they grant 1 extra Boon, it is more noteworthy that they let you take specialized Boons, ones not otherwise available to ANYONE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T13:51:42-07:00","id":1414259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1413002#post1413002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile for the Bogovi I\u2019m still unsure of but I do know I hate Veles, that line about stealing Scions\u2019 smartphones to teach them the world around them is more important is just peak boomer</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Look those gods who are a thousand years old or less are just spoiled and entitled. Back in my day we walked 10 miles in the snow uphill ot fight Titans.. then ten miles up hill in fire back... damn Millenials...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T14:06:16-07:00","id":1414262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414259#post1414259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Look those gods who are a thousand years old or less are just spoiled and entitled. Back in my day we walked 10 miles in the snow uphill ot fight Titans.. then ten miles up hill in fire back... damn Millenials...</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself wanting to have the Mesopotamic gods be like this with almost everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:20:06-07:00","id":1414295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414262#post1414262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find myself wanting to have the Mesopotamic gods be like this with almost everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>pretty much the Netjeru would be the only ones they couldn\u2019t pull it on (well... in secular time. Obviously retroactive mythic history makes lots of gods millions of years older than their first archeologically verified worshippers; and obviously that mythic chronologiy is simultaneously real too in the World).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-17-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:31:24-07:00","id":1414300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414295#post1414295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> pretty much the Netjeru would be the only ones they couldn\u2019t pull it on (well... in secular time. Obviously retroactive mythic history makes lots of gods millions of years older than their first archeologically verified worshippers; and obviously that mythic chronologiy is simultaneously real too in the World).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be sort of amusing if you had this club of various Semitic pantheons (Mesopotamians, Egyptians, Arabian, Canaanite/Carthaginian, Elamite, any others) who all look at the various Indo-European pantheons as juvenile uncivilized rubes from the sticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T19:16:24-07:00","id":1414314,"title":"","content":"Spoiled Millenial Pantheons don't even believe in Titans.. they say that's just a made up word. They don't know they are supposed to fear them. Fear the very word titan....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T07:43:42-07:00","id":1414398,"title":"","content":"I really like the Pachakutic Purview, it\u2019s innate is really beefy, I also like how the Boons interact with Sanctums","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T10:39:29-07:00","id":1414420,"title":"","content":"The Pachakutic Purview is awesome, and i primarily mean in the old sense of the word meaning &quot;Inspires Awe&quot;. Definitely a hefty PSP, and looking forward to the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T19:29:43-07:00","id":1414497,"title":"","content":"For me the charm of the Pachakutic Purview is its usefulness. Some 1e PSPs where very useful. The Greek and Japanese pantheons got the best. But many others where either too limited in scope or silly powerful. The Pachakutic Purview is potent without being overwhelming and, given the nature of the game, very useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T20:48:05-07:00","id":1414503,"title":"","content":"Demigod has a lot of 'places of power' magic stuff going on. Sancta (the plural of Sanctum), Realm Birthrights and at least one PSP...<br /> Very neat.<br /> <br /> I do hope when we get to the Underworld chapter, they provide us with Realm Knack examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T04:44:31-07:00","id":1414542,"title":"","content":"Chapter 4 manuscript\u201ds out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T08:24:41-07:00","id":1414568,"title":"","content":"Can someone provide a link to the errata page? I just saw a few little errors I wanted to point out in the Fatebinding section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T10:24:09-07:00","id":1414582,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The entire line is still to be released. As the guy posted above you can see where the projects stand. The text for Scion Origin was released to Kickstarter baskets about 6 months ago so we could keep catch spellings and inconsistencies and the like. Currently they are supposed to be putting the finally touches on Origin and I'm really hoping they give it to us before summer.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26355-wagonicfolding","name":"wagonicfolding","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T11:39:22-07:00","id":1414592,"title":"","content":"I love Dominion Boons, they do so much, they are definitely worth two Boon slots(even if they forgot to put that price in the preview by accident)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T11:50:34-07:00","id":1414594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wagonicfolding</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414582#post1414582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The entire line is still to be released. As the guy posted above you can see where the projects stand. The text for Scion Origin was released to Kickstarter baskets about 6 months ago so we could keep catch spellings and inconsistencies and the like. Currently they are supposed to be putting the finally touches on Origin and I'm really hoping they give it to us before summer.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>...Eh? Origin and Hero have already been released, and the books from the original KS shipped to backers. On top of that, we've got a jumpstart, ready-made characters, Mythical Denizens, Mysteries of the World, and Titanomachy all out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T11:58:59-07:00","id":1414597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wagonicfolding</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414582#post1414582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The entire line is still to be released. As the guy posted above you can see where the projects stand. The text for Scion Origin was released to Kickstarter baskets about 6 months ago so we could keep catch spellings and inconsistencies and the like. Currently they are supposed to be putting the finally touches on Origin and I'm really hoping they give it to us before summer.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo, not true. The first print was made with some missing errata, but it was released and it\u2019s not being worked. Origin, Hero, Mythic Denizens, Heroes of The World and A Light Extinguished are all final. The only book on Errata phase is Titanomachy (launched 2 weeks ago or so).<br /> <br /> Edit: I was writing when Marin posted, so, almost double post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T13:00:31-07:00","id":1414626,"title":"","content":"I just read the new Manuscript, and I am not sure if I understood right.<br /> <br /> If I understood right, all Demigod get <i>Casual Miracles</i> and the <i>Reduction of Marvel </i><i>Cost</i>, and those who get a Dominion just the <i>Dominion Boons</i> right? Or are the <i>Casual </i><i>Miracles </i>and <i>Reduction of Marvel Cost</i> just for those who get Dominion on that Purview?<br /> <br /> Thank you very much for your attention and help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 09-19-2020, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T13:17:45-07:00","id":1414628,"title":"","content":"You read as I did, but there are some missing information, that was explained in the discord.<br /> <br /> 1 Dominion occupy the space of 2 Boons.<br /> <br /> You pick 1 Dominion stunt per dominion you have that everyone can use in your team. If you have 2 dominions, you can pick both stunts from the same dominion and leave the other with no stunt.<br /> <br /> You can only use the reduction of marvel cost and casual miracles if you have dominion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T13:18:20-07:00","id":1414629,"title":"","content":"I know that casual miracles are for Dominion Boons, and I\u2019m pretty sure that the cheaper Marvels are for Purviews you have Dominion over","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T15:18:00-07:00","id":1414658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414628#post1414628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You read as I did, but there are some missing information, that was explained in the discord.<br /> <br /> 1 Dominion occupy the space of 2 Boons.<br /> <br /> You pick 1 Dominion stunt per dominion you have that everyone can use in your team. If you have 2 dominions, you can pick both stunts from the same dominion and leave the other with no stunt.<br /> <br /> You can only use the reduction of marvel cost and casual miracles if you have dominion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much, that makes all the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T18:49:19-07:00","id":1414676,"title":"","content":"I do hope the Companion will feature Demigod tier Relics what with the Relics stretch goal achieved. Relics for the new pantheons are nice, but it would be great to see examples of the powers Demigod Relics can have beyond what Hero Relics can do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T21:26:56-07:00","id":1414688,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Mortal failures </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">cause the character\u2019s divine nature to falter. If the roll fails and any of the </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">divinity dice are not successes, it provokes a mortal failure. Beyond </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">the roll failing, something </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">relevant to the rolling character\u2019s Purviews goes wildly out of control.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">If </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">a roll succeeds and no divinity dice show successes, or if a roll fails and some divinity dice </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">show successes, nothing spectacular happens. It is a suc</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">cess or failure as normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wait, which is it? If the roll fails, and <i>some but not all</i> divinity dice are successes, is it a mortal failure (because </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">&quot;any of the </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">divinity dice are not successes&quot;) or a normal failure (because some are successes)?<br /> <br /> I suspect the latter, because </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">&quot;any of the </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">divinity dice are not successes&quot; is oddly phrased so it seems likely to be a typo.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T04:31:13-07:00","id":1414712,"title":"","content":"The idea is:<br /> All divinity dice fail and you fail: Mortal Fail<br /> All divinity dice fail and you success: Normal Success<br /> Any divinity die success but not enough successes to beat difficulty: Normal Failure<br /> Any divinity die success and you success: Catastrophic success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T05:34:08-07:00","id":1414716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414628#post1414628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You read as I did, but there are some missing information, that was explained in the discord.<br /> <br /> 1 Dominion occupy the space of 2 Boons.<br /> <br /> You pick 1 Dominion stunt per dominion you have that everyone can use in your team. If you have 2 dominions, you can pick both stunts from the same dominion and leave the other with no stunt.<br /> <br /> You can only use the reduction of marvel cost and casual miracles if you have dominion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope this gets updated then, I'm not entirely clear how many, or just how in general a character gets Dominion and accesses these new powers. Don't get me wrong, they're really cool and I'm loving how they've expanded Demigods so they're not just &quot;Heroes with more book keeping&quot;. I'm not sure why we don't have a paragraph clearly explaining how many Dominions you get etc.<br /> <br /> First time I read it I thought it'd only affect the core Purview you pick at chargen, and now I unsure or confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T06:18:53-07:00","id":1414720,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure you get Dominion by swapping out two Boons whenever you get an increase in Legend, similar to normal Boon swapping. Also I\u2019ve done the math and the maximum Dominions a Demigod can have, at Legend 8 is 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T06:22:16-07:00","id":1414721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414720#post1414720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure you get Dominion by swapping out two Boons whenever you get an increase in Legend, similar to normal Boon swapping. Also I\u2019ve done the math and the maximum Dominions a Demigod can have, at Legend 8 is 4</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right thanks! Where did you read that? I've resorted to ctrl-F-ing the preview documents for dominion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T06:35:10-07:00","id":1414727,"title":"","content":"The two Boon slots is from what Neall has said, he explained in the discord that the cost for Dominions being left out was a mistake and should be reported in the Errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T09:04:39-07:00","id":1414745,"title":"","content":"So I think we've got enough of the book that I have to ask, is it intended that even at the demigod level Scions can only draw on one purview and their PSP without a relic or guide? It just feels a little strange to me that one can have Dominion over Fire and Forge, but if one of them comes from a relic you lose or a guide you upset, suddenly this big concept you have influence over is lost to you.<br /> <br /> Edit: and an unrelated question: how does the reduced Marvel cost for Dominion work with emulating Boons? Is it unchanged? If spending legend turns into imbue legend across the board, then can you just emulate any Boon that costs imbued Legend your motifs will allow at no increased cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12145-arion-wind","user":"Arion Wind","date":". 09-20-2020, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12145-arion-wind","name":"Arion Wind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T09:30:12-07:00","id":1414749,"title":"","content":"Look, even Thor lost his hammer once and had to go get it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T09:32:35-07:00","id":1414750,"title":"","content":"So I keep seeing mention to a Discord. How do I gain access to this mythical place of information and like minded people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T10:54:23-07:00","id":1414761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414750#post1414750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I keep seeing mention to a Discord. How do I gain access to this mythical place of information and like minded people?</div> </div> </div> </div>At The Onyx Path home page on the right side, above the red bubble add, there is an icon like Mikey Mouse pants, just click there and you will be invited to OPP Discord Server.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T10:56:10-07:00","id":1414762,"title":"","content":"While not mentioned, my reading is that the reduced cost of marvels would imply on emulating boons costing as much as the original boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T15:03:29-07:00","id":1414823,"title":"","content":"So does anyone else think the collateral pool is a bit too punishing? While I initially liked it, as I started thinking on it it feels more like a punishment on the players for using their abilities. At the very least I\u2019d be more okay with it if there were less GENERAL ways to increase it, like if only certain types of Scale increased it, or if only certain types of Marvels increased it. But right now it feels like it\u2019s just punishing the players just for using their tools","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T15:24:36-07:00","id":1414827,"title":"","content":"I take the collateral pool as a get ye to have the Demigods to vacate areas where it is likely to go off. If a Demigod starts throwing around combat miracles in the middle of a city, I can see the property values plummet. For procedural play, I can see Echoes contaminate clues, but I would probably avoid using the Harm stunt.<br /> <br /> Just checking that every Demigod gets divinity dice? Because the way they are listed under Dominion implies otherwise to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T15:31:18-07:00","id":1414828,"title":"","content":"Yes every Demigod gets Divinity Dice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T15:41:58-07:00","id":1414832,"title":"","content":"*Adding the Collateral Pool to as many games as possible*<br /> <br /> Punishing? I think you mean &quot;Ways to keep this SPICY&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T06:47:08-07:00","id":1414909,"title":"","content":"Hi all! I had a question about Fatebinding. According to the preview, a demigod <i>must</i> attend to their fatebinding once each <i>session</i>, or face the Avoidance consequences. Given that a demigod can have a significant number of fatebindings, and that parties are encouraged to be several players, how does each session become anything <i>other</i> than dealing with everyone's bindings (either attending to them, or dealing with the consequences)? Or am I reading this wrong? Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11206-maheshwarastra","name":"maheshwarastra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T07:32:56-07:00","id":1414912,"title":"","content":"And some of the results the SG can choose are not necessarily directly harmful. They can be attention-getting instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T08:46:21-07:00","id":1414921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414823#post1414823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does anyone else think the collateral pool is a bit too punishing? While I initially liked it, as I started thinking on it it feels more like a punishment on the players for using their abilities. At the very least I\u2019d be more okay with it if there were less GENERAL ways to increase it, like if only certain types of Scale increased it, or if only certain types of Marvels increased it. But right now it feels like it\u2019s just punishing the players just for using their tools</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I need to reread the Scion rules closely, but the Aberrant version notes that they're not necessarily physically destructive. You can use collateral pool for the social change consequences of your actions, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-21-2020, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T09:11:37-07:00","id":1414928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maheshwarastra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414909#post1414909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all! I had a question about Fatebinding. According to the preview, a demigod <i>must</i> attend to their fatebinding once each <i>session</i>, or face the Avoidance consequences. Given that a demigod can have a significant number of fatebindings, and that parties are encouraged to be several players, how does each session become anything <i>other</i> than dealing with everyone's bindings (either attending to them, or dealing with the consequences)? Or am I reading this wrong? Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong, but honestly, that should likely be maintenance of <i>one </i>Fatebinding per session and it should be forgiving for an event that takes up the entire session. I may amend that rule and then work it back into solo/troupe play, where yeah you <i>should </i>take care of everything in one session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T22:14:10-07:00","id":1415016,"title":"","content":"More seriously, re: Scion's Collateral Pool, some of them are destructive (Razing things, injuries) while some are social (People angry that you aren't containing the destruction) and some are kinda destructive but in a way that I think leads to more Story Fun than blowing shit up (Let loose with your Purview via Echo, and then Rift for &quot;Oops a portal opened up&quot;), and some that are obvious but not as destructive (Pinning and knocking Extras out of the scene)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T02:07:59-07:00","id":1415030,"title":"","content":"Quick question for the Divinity Dice: Besides Catastrophic Success, Mortal Failure and Flooding the Pool, do they have any other mechanical effect? I'm just basing it off how the section for Defense notes that Defense rolls using Divinity Dice reroll 9's. Is this the case with all Divinity Dice or only in this specific instance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T06:18:40-07:00","id":1415056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1414928#post1414928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not wrong, but honestly, that should likely be maintenance of <i>one </i>Fatebinding per session and it should be forgiving for an event that takes up the entire session. I may amend that rule and then work it back into solo/troupe play, where yeah you <i>should </i>take care of everything in one session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the quick reply! It turns out that I was reading it incorrectly, and missed the &quot;<i>at least one</i>&quot; part. So there is a lot to do with many players, but not as much as I feared. Certainly, solo/low player number games should play fatebindings more often so that the player has more to do. Sorry for missing that. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11206-maheshwarastra","name":"maheshwarastra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T06:52:06-07:00","id":1415185,"title":"","content":"So I\u2019m reading the new chapter and does anyone else notice the Tengri and Apu ones missing? Like there\u2019s nothing on them here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T13:25:42-07:00","id":1415233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415185#post1415185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I\u2019m reading the new chapter and does anyone else notice the Tengri and Apu ones missing? Like there\u2019s nothing on them here</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that is the case. Hopefully that'll be put in, and if not, we have the Veil; Erlik wouldn't mind that place.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, that is an awesome concept; it's literally the Pure Afterlife, devoid of any Pantheon and yet vital to them all, because it's the middle ground. No wonder Liminal sorts like it, it's a place where everyone can build their confidence before walking the path.<br /> <br /> The Yazata Underworlds are cool too - I always like the High Psychodrama of &quot;reliving your life&quot;, and of course the Pantheon with Free Will as a virtue has &quot;second chance&quot; as an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T13:38:03-07:00","id":1415234,"title":"","content":"Looks like there's a stretch goal to put the missing underworlds in the companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T16:10:42-07:00","id":1415243,"title":"","content":"Not specifically Underworlds. The new stretch goal states Terra Incognita, so they could well be Midrealms, or even 'overworlds'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T16:17:25-07:00","id":1415245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415185#post1415185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I\u2019m reading the new chapter and does anyone else notice the Tengri and Apu ones missing? Like there\u2019s nothing on them here</div> </div> </div> </div>No Bogovi Underworld either. But as said already, hopefully that gets fixed in the Companion with the Terra Incognita stretch goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","name":"demonchilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T17:29:05-07:00","id":1415249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415243#post1415243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not specifically Underworlds. The new stretch goal states Terra Incognita, so they could well be Midrealms, or even 'overworlds'.</div> </div> </div> </div>MUST. HAVE. <br /> <br /> Seriously, I want more Terra Incognita. Everyone go round up random people off the street and get them to pledge. Offer snacks if you have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T18:41:52-07:00","id":1415258,"title":"","content":"I'd bet we'll end up close to $140k. So, at least one Terra Incognitae stretch goal should be reached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T21:54:25-07:00","id":1415264,"title":"","content":"While the Underworld for the Manitou is overall good content, the section on \u201cOther Manitou\u201d could use another pass; it manages to be both repetitive of the content about the Manitou in Hero and simultaneously changes the naming conventions.<br /> <br /> (And that\u2019s without getting into how there\u2019s one Underwater Panther in Hero and Titanomachy, but lots of them in Demigod, or how there\u2019s one Horned Serpent in Titanomachy but lots of them in Hero and Demigod. If they keep separating and condensing again, they\u2019ll make poor Aniwye jealous!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T02:41:17-07:00","id":1415281,"title":"","content":"Overworlds will be presented in details in God, as it\u2019s literally where they live, and we need to understand more about how gods manifest before understanding where they live.<br /> <br /> But yes, Under and mid realms are a great stretch goals!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T03:11:56-07:00","id":1415517,"title":"","content":"I was re-reading the Demigod book so far, and when re-reading the part about the Path to Apotheosis to Take/Share a Mantle, it says you need to make so each Milestone on the path is related to the Myth of the god in question. So far so good, but it also says a demigod may change their mind midway, deciding to either make their own Mantle or taking someone else`s. How would it work?<br /> <br /> Like, lets say after 3 Milestones, a player decides they want to now become the new Dagda, do they only need to do 1 Milestone imitating Dagda`s myths (as the last one would be the whole fighting him for the Mantle)? Or should they do 5 quick misadventures to do the five myths? Or are the player, at this point, unable to change their mind (Basically, you can change your mind <i>from </i>taking/sharing a mantle, but not <i>to</i> taking/sharing a mantle)?<br /> <br /> Thank you very much for your attention and help, hope you have a nice day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T12:44:00-07:00","id":1415719,"title":"","content":"Finally getting to sit down and really read all of the previews. Good stuff.<br /> <br /> One questions: are the Anunna and the Apu actually meant to have the exact same asset skills of Culture and Leadership? I mean, it works thematically since they're both ambitious, empire-building Pantheons. Just kind of funny that happened to two Pantheons in the same edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","name":"Doryna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T13:38:27-07:00","id":1415730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415517#post1415517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was re-reading the Demigod book so far, and when re-reading the part about the Path to Apotheosis to Take/Share a Mantle, it says you need to make so each Milestone on the path is related to the Myth of the god in question. So far so good, but it also says a demigod may change their mind midway, deciding to either make their own Mantle or taking someone else`s. How would it work?<br /> <br /> Like, lets say after 3 Milestones, a player decides they want to now become the new Dagda, do they only need to do 1 Milestone imitating Dagda`s myths (as the last one would be the whole fighting him for the Mantle)? Or should they do 5 quick misadventures to do the five myths? Or are the player, at this point, unable to change their mind (Basically, you can change your mind <i>from </i>taking/sharing a mantle, but not <i>to</i> taking/sharing a mantle)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That's a good question and one that I didn't consider when I was writing that bit, so thanks for bringing it up. I'd be inclined that, after a few Milestones, you could decide to swerve <i>away</i> from a God's Mantle, but not into one. Taking on an existing Mantle feels like something you commit to right from the start, or at best after you've completed the Second Call. (Although I'm sure there will be cases where a character accidentally stumbles onto a path imitating a God's without fully realizing it, only to be nearly done and think, &quot;Oh, no... I might be Gilgamesh.&quot;)<br /> <br /> -g.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T14:06:40-07:00","id":1415733,"title":"","content":"Question on Dominion. Do scions gain dominion to any purview they have access too? Sorry my brain just is not processing right now and I\u2019ve read through and it does not really call out, that I can see, how demigods gain dominion other then when they hit demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T15:46:13-07:00","id":1415751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415733#post1415733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on Dominion. Do scions gain dominion to any purview they have access too? Sorry my brain just is not processing right now and I\u2019ve read through and it does not really call out, that I can see, how demigods gain dominion other then when they hit demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently that was an error. You are meant to opt into Dominion by spending two 'Boon slots' on it. While this can theoretically be done with any Purview you have access too, you don't automatically gain Dominion in every one of your Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T18:29:23-07:00","id":1415767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doryna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415719#post1415719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally getting to sit down and really read all of the previews. Good stuff.<br /> <br /> One questions: are the Anunna and the Apu actually meant to have the exact same asset skills of Culture and Leadership? I mean, it works thematically since they're both ambitious, empire-building Pantheons. Just kind of funny that happened to two Pantheons in the same edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>If culture and leadership are interpreted in profoundly different ways, it's no problem. And they would be. Just look at the profound difference between the meaning of those words for John C. Calhoun and Jefferson Davis on the one hand and FDR and Harry Truman on the other. Both are pairs of prominent American men working in the government. But can you imagine them agreeing on definition of leadership and culture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T00:28:20-07:00","id":1415784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415767#post1415767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If culture and leadership are interpreted in profoundly different ways, it's no problem. And they would be. Just look at the profound difference between the meaning of those words for John C. Calhoun and Jefferson Davis on the one hand and FDR and Harry Truman on the other. Both are pairs of prominent American men working in the government. But can you imagine them agreeing on definition of leadership and culture?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Culture is less about being smart and refined and more about being an experienced traveler and well-read in the ways of others. It\u2019s the skill for courtesy, fitting in, and knowing the ins and outs of other cultures, important for globetrotting Scions.<br /> <br /> In fact, four out of the five Demigod pantheons have Culture as an Asset Skill, three of them associated with empire and rulership of disparate peoples (the Apu, Annuna, and Tengri) and two with aggressive syncretism and adaptability (the Bogovi and Tengri, again).<br /> <br /> At this point, Culture may be the most common Asset Skill, given that it\u2019s also under the umbrella of the Kami, the Teotl and the Tuatha de Danann.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T17:45:50-07:00","id":1415908,"title":"","content":"Something I hope that\u2019s in the Demigod Companion expansion for Cults and Covenants is discussion on having nations or governments as a Cult, cause the Cult system does a surprisingly good job at mechanically representing organizations in general already, so it feels like with some upgrades it would be a proper fit for mechanically representing \u201cdivine king of x\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T09:27:14-07:00","id":1415994,"title":"","content":"New manuscript preview out! Loving the new antagonist rules and the Gods who refused the Keepers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T09:46:25-07:00","id":1416002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raz_Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1415784#post1415784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that Culture is less about being smart and refined and more about being an experienced traveler and well-read in the ways of others. It\u2019s the skill for courtesy, fitting in, and knowing the ins and outs of other cultures, important for globetrotting Scions.<br /> <br /> In fact, four out of the five Demigod pantheons have Culture as an Asset Skill, three of them associated with empire and rulership of disparate peoples (the Apu, Annuna, and Tengri) and two with aggressive syncretism and adaptability (the Bogovi and Tengri, again).<br /> <br /> At this point, Culture may be the most common Asset Skill, given that it\u2019s also under the umbrella of the Kami, the Teotl and the Tuatha de Danann.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well put. I also noticed that as I was reading through the rest of the new pantheons. I've always interpreted Culture in Scion similarly to you, and as I said, it makes sense, especially for Pantheons steeped in globetrotting and empire-building. Just found it interesting that as different as the Annuna and the Apu are in terms of their own cultures, they have very similar values. As Astromancer said above, it's up to each Pantheon's own interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","name":"Doryna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T12:06:18-07:00","id":1416016,"title":"","content":"Yaaaay Tlazolteotl is back! Love the Keepers of the World bit overall","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T12:16:32-07:00","id":1416017,"title":"","content":"Quick question, is Geasa supposed to get deadlier in demigod/god? For heroic scions breaking a geasa means losing legend points. Is it more dangerous for demigods/gods? The example apotheosis story has the main character threaten to place a geasa on a god if he doesn't appear. If it is just the loss of legend points he could just sulk in a sanctum for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/670-wyrdwise","name":"Wyrdwise","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T12:48:09-07:00","id":1416021,"title":"","content":"Doesn\u2019t seem like it, but if you want you could go with what\u2019s in the sagas themselves where breaking a Geas regardless of who you are, outright kills you or gives you such a debilitating condition of some kind that you\u2019re probably gonna die soon anyways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T13:13:34-07:00","id":1416022,"title":"","content":"Nothing more at Demigod level but we know Fate grows sharper teeth again at God level, and I think pantheon specific metaphysical weaknesses have been floated - it would not surprise me at all if the way to permanently kill a TDD is if they\u2019re in Geas violation (as opposed to their normal deaths they can come back from in the next scene).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T14:45:51-07:00","id":1416027,"title":"","content":"In honor of the Appendix, I present the Keeper of the World National Anthem:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dyne7jtuKr8\" data-code=\"Dyne7jtuKr8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Dyne7jtuKr8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T14:49:43-07:00","id":1416029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1416027#post1416027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In honor of the Appendix, I present the Keeper of the World National Anthem:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dyne7jtuKr8\" data-code=\"Dyne7jtuKr8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Dyne7jtuKr8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought this was going to be Imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T16:37:22-07:00","id":1416045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1416029#post1416029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought this was going to be Imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel that there's enough problems with the plan to have Imhotep a little hesitant about whether he's thought through all of it.<br /> <br /> If Zalmoxis does become the Top God, it could easily be this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/u1WZgAiVxl4\" data-code=\"u1WZgAiVxl4\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/u1WZgAiVxl4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T21:20:36-07:00","id":1416053,"title":"","content":"Notably, the antagonists chapter uses the terminology from Hero for the Thunderbirds, \u201cAnimikii,\u201d rather than \u201cbinesi\u201d from the Underworld chapter. That antagonist entry slots in really well with Hero, tbh.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a bit odd that Omukade is here again as \u201cgiant centipedes\u201d when it was a singular monster with a different stat block in Titanomachy. Like, I don\u2019t mind being given multiple takes on a critter, but I\u2019d prefer a mindful inconsistency in the line, and direct encouragement to go with either or both as you see fit.<br /> <br /> The Keepers appendix is phenomenal. The idea always had real estate in my head since 1e, but this is a version of the Keepers easily able to be slotted into different roles on a game\u2014 even as divine parents, which is delightful. Adding in Karna and Amergin? Inspired. Zalmoxis might as well be wearing a sticker that says \u201cloosely inspired by real mythology,\u201d but at least he\u2019s <i>interesting.</i> Stellar take on Herakles, Tlaz\u014dte\u014dtl\u2019s back, and Wayland Smith is appropriately scary. Just, wow. What a note to end the book on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T08:27:19-07:00","id":1416105,"title":"","content":"Confucius's reason for not wanting to be a Keeper made me smile and chuckle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T10:18:04-07:00","id":1416124,"title":"","content":"I'm including a new Keeper in one of my Pantheon fanprojects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T03:24:55-07:00","id":1416220,"title":"","content":"Quick question; how do you determine the effects of a Mortal Failure or a Catastrophic Success? I don't mean when they occur (fail a rolled action and Divinity Dice show at least one failure or succeed on a rolled action and Divinity dice show at least one success, respectively) but how you determine what the outcome looks like.<br /> The classic example is instead of convincing the town to back you on *insert issue here*, you convince the nation. But how did you determine the scale? Why the nation and not the state/province? What does it look like when you make Catastrophic Success on a Boon roll?<br /> And can I have an example of a Mortal Failure please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T05:27:15-07:00","id":1416230,"title":"","content":"Are there even Boon rolls? Anyways isn\u2019t that what the catastrophic success/mortal failures sections under each Purview in chapter 4 are for? To give examples of what they look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T09:18:11-07:00","id":1416279,"title":"","content":"I figure that Catastrophic Successes often draw from having Dominion in some ways, since they represent your power running amok. Most Boons don't even have rolls, at least not to activate them. Like if you make a roll and it benefits from a Dominion Stunt, that may flavor it.<br /> <br /> Even if you're not touching a Dominion Boon directly, I figure the power may bleed through just by having Dominion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T11:13:22-07:00","id":1416308,"title":"","content":"And we made it! 143k!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T10:09:58-07:00","id":1416491,"title":"","content":"Will it be on backerkit II Kinda sorta missed kickstartter<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T10:31:23-07:00","id":1416495,"title":"","content":"Yeah, probably in about a month or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T18:58:45-07:00","id":1416663,"title":"","content":"I just finished Demigod. I loved the Keepers of the World, but I couldn\u2019t find the write-ups for the Irish Demigod Cu Chulainn or the Palas (Tibetan) pantheon. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T19:12:58-07:00","id":1416664,"title":"","content":"The Palas were never slated to be IN Demigod, unfortunately. Maybe God?<br /> <br /> I admit I was under the impression that we'd have writeups for CuChulainn or Gilgamesh for playing them reborn, and I didn't spot them either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T22:12:16-07:00","id":1416684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1416664#post1416664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Palas were never slated to be IN Demigod, unfortunately. Maybe God?<br /> <br /> I admit I was under the impression that we'd have writeups for CuChulainn or Gilgamesh for playing them reborn, and I didn't spot them either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is unfortunate. I want to have them fight. And then turn into some sort of weird super-Shonen tsundere BL couple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T22:46:51-07:00","id":1416685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1416684#post1416684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is unfortunate. I want to have them fight. And then turn into some sort of weird super-Shonen tsundere BL couple.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see you too have been partaking of certain Fate/Stay Night materials... but seriously, having a list of &quot;Reincarnations&quot; that would list Callings and Purviews for them would be great to have, even as a minor supplement. I've got a friend whose trying to stat up a reincarnation of Jason and something like that would be really helpful for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T23:59:15-07:00","id":1416690,"title":"","content":"Okay, need to clarify my earlier question; IF you don't take a Dominion, how do Mortal Failures and Catastrophic Successes work? And how do you try to moderate the scale of the effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T00:49:37-07:00","id":1416694,"title":"","content":"I think they work the same even if you don\u2019t have Dominion, you pick the Purview that most makes sense with your action and go with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T06:09:04-07:00","id":1416715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1416664#post1416664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Palas were never slated to be IN Demigod, unfortunately. Maybe God?<br /> <br /> I admit I was under the impression that we'd have writeups for CuChulainn or Gilgamesh for playing them reborn, and I didn't spot them either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T10:48:41-07:00","id":1416740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1416690#post1416690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, need to clarify my earlier question; IF you don't take a Dominion, how do Mortal Failures and Catastrophic Successes work? And how do you try to moderate the scale of the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pick a way that your success can go Super Intense, relating to one's Title or their Omen. Pick a way that your failure can be over the top. The Mortal Failures or Catastrophic Successes are not EXCLUSIVELY tied to Dominion. Like, in Chapter 4 it just says that Catastrophic Successes are when the success is above and beyond, and Mortal Failures are when things go awry, with also a note about one of your Purviews going amok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T01:25:28-07:00","id":1416955,"title":"","content":"I really like the Keepers, they make fantastic antagonists. In that you can clearly see and sympathize with why they came to the conclusions they did, while also understanding why they\u2019re in the wrong and why they need to be stopped","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T06:03:18-07:00","id":1416978,"title":"","content":"I like the Keepers too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T10:31:32-07:00","id":1417018,"title":"","content":"Yeah, other than tweaking Heracles' Purviews, and giving Zalmoxis a solo-God Path usable for Zalmoxis Scion PCs, I don't see anything I'd change! Which is huge given the disaster that the Keepers were in 1E (admittedly 90% was Cortes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T11:38:39-07:00","id":1417026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417018#post1417018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, other than tweaking Heracles' Purviews, and giving Zalmoxis a solo-God Path usable for Zalmoxis Scion PCs, I don't see anything I'd change! Which is huge given the disaster that the Keepers were in 1E (admittedly 90% was Cortes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Cortes was a good idea. Making him a pawn in a fight between gods who then dumped him when they had no further use for him was also a good idea. Making Cortes a depressive seeking suicide was a bad idea. Cortes would have sought vengeance not self destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T12:53:01-07:00","id":1417043,"title":"","content":"Making Cortez the Scion of Quetzalcoatl was a very bad idea as well, since it gives validation to the myth that Cortez was considered a god when he first encountered the Aztecs(which wasn\u2019t true, that\u2019s a lie he made and his allies made up) and also gives validation to the other lie that colonialism and it\u2019s various genocides were divinely mandated or justified","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 10-06-2020, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T13:49:02-07:00","id":1417048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417026#post1417026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cortes was a good idea. Making him a pawn in a fight between gods who then dumped him when they had no further use for him was also a good idea. Making Cortes a depressive seeking suicide was a bad idea. Cortes would have sought vengeance not self destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, look, we've had our heated moments and I don't want to turn this into a shitshow, so I'll just say my piece and not respond further on this topic.<br /> <br /> No. Making Cortes a keeper was a <b>fucking terrible idea</b> that at best was incredibly tone deaf, and at worst was giving legitimacy to Spain's invasion of the Aztec Empire. ESPECIALLY making him a Scion with the blessing and aim of ONE OF THE AZTEC PEOPLE'S OWN GODS, who sent Cortes there (which resulted in, to bluntly remind, the slaughter and subjugation of an entire culture) to 'purge the corruption' because the Aztec people had grown terrible and in need of a downfall thanks to Tezcatlipoca's influence.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't even take much reading to get the implication of &quot;The one Aztec God we wrote in 1e as not being a totally horrible monster with the personality of Khorne from 40k <i><b>literally blessed the invasion that led to the subjugation and slaughter of his own culture</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Cortes doesn't deserve any kind of vindication. Cortes doesn't deserve any kind of historical revisionism to paint him as anything but what he was: A greedy stupid shortsighted man who led an army that committed terrible atrocities. And if you're going to give him divine backing, don't make it <i>the Gods of the people whom he killed</i>. There's a reason people don't claim that the Hindu Gods actually led England to its subjugation of India, nor that they claim that the many gods of the North American native tribes invited the English Settlers to form the modern USA. Because doing that is tantamount to saying &quot;Hey, people who got fucked by imperialism: Your Gods blessed this&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is not a sentence ANYBODY should write, or imply. Now I'll mention here that <i>I am not accusing anybody of deliberately encouraging these ideas nor am I accusing anybody of being racist</i>, I'm just noting that sometimes people write or say things and don't think through the implications of what they went with. I'm fully certain that the writers of the Keepers in 1e wanted to write a cool story, and that if this were explained out to them they'd be horrified. People make mistakes, and I'm not going to accuse any kind of deeper malice without knowing.<br /> <br /> But no, no. Cortes as a Keeper was a TERRIBLE idea that never should have been done, and it never SHOULD be done. Let Cortes be a pathetic individual who has the blood of an entire culture on his hands.<br /> <br /> So, to change the subject... I'm running a Hero game and I may bend some of the rules for allowing Realm Birthrights, as I recently sent my players into the realm of Hades, one of whom is a Scion of Persephone, and getting her Fatebound to the realm would be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-06-2020, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T14:19:33-07:00","id":1417050,"title":"","content":"Ooo that sounds fun! Realm Birthrights are really cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T14:44:04-07:00","id":1417053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417050#post1417050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooo that sounds fun! Realm Birthrights are really cool</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconded! And it makes sense since some deities (generally those more important in Myth than religion) are very tied to/ a reflection of their realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T14:59:35-07:00","id":1417058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417048#post1417048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, look, we've had our heated moments and I don't want to turn this into a shitshow, so I'll just say my piece and not respond further on this topic.<br /> <br /> No. Making Cortes a keeper was a <b>fucking terrible idea</b> that at best was incredibly tone deaf, and at worst was giving legitimacy to Spain's invasion of the Aztec Empire. ESPECIALLY making him a Scion with the blessing and aim of ONE OF THE AZTEC PEOPLE'S OWN GODS, who sent Cortes there (which resulted in, to bluntly remind, the slaughter and subjugation of an entire culture) to 'purge the corruption' because the Aztec people had grown terrible and in need of a downfall thanks to Tezcatlipoca's influence.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't even take much reading to get the implication of &quot;The one Aztec God we wrote in 1e as not being a totally horrible monster with the personality of Khorne from 40k <i><b>literally blessed the invasion that led to the subjugation and slaughter of his own culture</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I make a distinction between history and fiction. I also note that Cortes got vast numbers of Native American allies because even those Mexicans that had some vague idea of the horrors of Spanish rule (a larger group than most might think) greatly preferred the devil they didn't know. The Aztecs were the most glamourous and interesting tribe/nation in Mexico, not the only group in Mexico. Many Native Mexicans praised Cortes to their dying days in spite of his being a monster because they hated the Aztecs more. <br /> <br /> Note: Historically, the Aztecs did say in many separate documents that they mistook Cortez for Quetzalcoatl. Which is one reason why some scholars now think Quetzalcoatl was made up as an excuse by the Aztec elites for being taken in by Cortes. Myself, I'd want to see their evidence before I dismiss Quetzalcoatl as mere fiction. <br /> <br /> That said, we will let this drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T15:12:28-07:00","id":1417062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417058#post1417058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I make a distinction between history and fiction. I also note that Cortes got vast numbers of Native American allies because even those Mexicans that had some vague idea of the horrors of Spanish rule (a larger group than most might think) greatly preferred the devil they didn't know. The Aztecs were the most glamourous and interesting tribe/nation in Mexico, not the only group in Mexico. Many Native Mexicans praised Cortes to their dying days in spite of his being a monster because they hated the Aztecs more.<br /> <br /> Note: Historically, the Aztecs did say in many separate documents that they mistook Cortez for Quetzalcoatl. Which is one reason why some scholars now think Quetzalcoatl was made up as an excuse by the Aztec elites for being taken in by Cortes. Myself, I'd want to see their evidence before I dismiss Quetzalcoatl as mere fiction.<br /> <br /> That said, we will let this drop.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise a valid point that the Aztecs were not defeated by Cortez and were, in fact, a tyrannical dictatorship hated by the surrounding peoples they oppressed. It is only revisionist history that eliminates the brave souls who rose up against them because Cortez played the role of Roose Bolton and immediately betrayed his &quot;allies&quot; to impose his own brutal tyranny.<br /> <br /> But this runs a bit to Cortez apologia and he was a real piece of shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-08-2020, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T15:36:09-07:00","id":1417067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417062#post1417062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You raise a valid point that the Aztecs were not defeated by Cortez and were, in fact, a tyrannical dictatorship hated by the surrounding peoples they oppressed. It is only revisionist history that eliminates the brave souls who rose up against them because Cortez played the role of Roose Bolton and immediately betrayed his &quot;allies&quot; to impose his own brutal tyranny.<br /> <br /> But this runs a bit to Cortez apologia and he was a real piece of shit.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't say he wasn't. I pointed out that Cortes was a monster. I only pointed out that many people hated the Aztecs more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T15:37:27-07:00","id":1417069,"title":"","content":"Not entering a discussion, hence the red text, just letting some factoids of the &quot;official position&quot; be known here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T15:59:47-07:00","id":1417073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417069#post1417069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not entering a discussion, hence the red text, just letting some factoids of the &quot;official position&quot; be known here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry if I misunderstood your focus. I don't want to make your job harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T16:33:05-07:00","id":1417076,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the drafts yet (vision issues make reading large pdf files problematic for me), so I'm curious if there's anything about possibilities of Heroes who become Demigods creating legends that start to break them away from their originating pantheon? Like, just to invent a random example, say a Scion of Hades devoted to wealth and money raises himself up to Demigod status, but as the newly christened &quot;Mammon&quot;, a lot of his Legend seems tied up in Renaissance/early Enlightenment era European folklore rather than with anything to do with the Theoi. Or Columbia as a Scion of Athena becoming more connected to 19th century Americana than to Greek myth. Or is this the sort of thing that God is more likely to be dealing with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T16:54:31-07:00","id":1417081,"title":"","content":"Forging one's own Mantle is forging one's own Mantle. It doesn't really say a lot about going from a Demigod in a Pantheon to becoming Independent, but I'd allow it for taking a Deed to reflect forging a Covenant, and then a major Deed for officially breaking away from their original Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T19:46:08-07:00","id":1417091,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall one of the 'bad guy' scions in First Edition taking on the role of Santa Muerte. Granted, it was at god level, but I don't see why a scion couldn't decide earlier on to go for it and to model themselves after a vacant role or an image outside of their own and basically 'faking it until you make it'. After all, you are what you do in Scion. There's no reason you couldn't get an early start, and the RP options would be awesome. Can you imagine Hades popping in on the would-be Mammon with a 'Son, we need to talk about your career choices.' talk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T04:47:35-07:00","id":1417303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417076#post1417076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the drafts yet (vision issues make reading large pdf files problematic for me), so I'm curious if there's anything about possibilities of Heroes who become Demigods creating legends that start to break them away from their originating pantheon? Like, just to invent a random example, say a Scion of Hades devoted to wealth and money raises himself up to Demigod status, but as the newly christened &quot;Mammon&quot;, a lot of his Legend seems tied up in Renaissance/early Enlightenment era European folklore rather than with anything to do with the Theoi. Or Columbia as a Scion of Athena becoming more connected to 19th century Americana than to Greek myth. Or is this the sort of thing that God is more likely to be dealing with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be more God-level play; the section on the Keeper's of the World describes their plan as a Creation Myth for a new pantheon.<br /> Demigods do get to define their divine identity by creating their own Mantles, but tying themselves to a new culture or people is both not strictly present in Demigod, (though the Covenant birthright is still a thing), and it defiantly fits God better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T11:18:09-07:00","id":1417344,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see why a Demigod couldn\u2019t try to remove themselves from a pantheon, probably wouldn\u2019t be easy but there\u2019s nothing stopping you from doing that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T04:35:07-07:00","id":1417428,"title":"","content":"I have a question, all Immortal Knacks described in Scion Demigod can only be purchased by Demigod or Scions of Hero level can buy then too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T04:43:38-07:00","id":1417429,"title":"","content":"Only Demigods. I would make them a new category as they are really better than other Immortal knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T07:04:13-07:00","id":1417437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411612-scion-2e-demigod-kickstarter?p=1417429#post1417429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only Demigods. I would make them a new category as they are really better than other Immortal knacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what you think or it's something written in the manuscript? Or an unnoficial errata mentioned by the devs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T07:59:19-07:00","id":1417446,"title":"","content":"The paragraph on Immortal Knacks (page 160 of the new all in one manuscript) says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As your character progresses from Hero to Demigod, their Callings and Legendary Titles become true forces of nature. A Demigod can throw the weight of their divinity around to influence The World just as a giant might utilize their size. A wider variety of Knacks are available that allow you to Imbue for Scale: (...) </div> </div> </div>I read this as \u201cDemigods have access to those, and Heroes don\u2019t\u201d, but I may be wrong...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T08:01:34-07:00","id":1417447,"title":"","content":"They're just described as Immortal Knacks and I think I saw a comment from Neall on a discord that they're open for Heroes to buy. I mean, most of the Knacks aren't much stronger than any other Heroic Knacks, just more versatile.<br /> <br /> (I did submit some errata for clarity though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T08:47:02-07:00","id":1417457,"title":"","content":"Yeah Neall has said on the Discord that they\u2019re available to Heroes, which makes sense since most of them aren\u2019t any better then Hero Immortal Knacks and instead are more meant to give mechanical support for the other aspects of Callings(and of course there\u2019s Size Them Up, which is Heroic in it\u2019s effects)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T15:32:19-07:00","id":1417718,"title":"","content":"So, quick question about creating Relics through Fatebinding ordinary items: Beyond the standard maximum number of Fatebindings a character can have, is there any limit/cost to creating Relics this way, such as paying XP for the initial dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T15:48:49-07:00","id":1417721,"title":"","content":"Hmm doesn\u2019t seem like it, it seems like just an expansion of that mechanic of gaining another character\u2019s Relic at the cost of getting a Fatebinding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}